# AI working documentation

Paired hard rule: every iteration must also update **ai-knowledge** (skills + recipes + `pnpm knowledge:sync`). See `.cursor/rules/ai-knowledge-sync.mdc`.

## Three buckets (`_ai-docs/`)

| Bucket | Path | Rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| WIP | `_ai-docs/wip/<topic>/` | Ephemeral — **delete after promote** |
| Brainstorm | `_ai-docs/brainstorm/` | Package names/improvements — **not** implementation scratch |
| Audit | `_ai-docs/audit/` | Point-in-time quality snapshot |

**Planning what to build** → `roadmap/` (priorities, horizon, backlog). Do not add `platform-roadmap/` or root-level topic folders.

## While working (WIP only)

1. Create `_ai-docs/wip/<topic>/` from `_ai-docs/_template/overview.md` (frontmatter: status, promotes-to, skills, recipes).
2. Notes must be **good enough to draft public docs**: problem, decisions, APIs, edge cases, migration, **and** which skills/recipes change.
3. Prefer ≤4 files (`overview.md`, optional `decisions.md`, `api.md`, `migration.md`) — no scatter.
4. Same iteration: update package docs + Intent skills; update `recipes.yaml` when discoverable; run `pnpm knowledge:sync` / `knowledge:check`.

## When the user says work is finished

1. Promote into real docs:
   - Package guides: `packages/<category>/<name>/docs/`
   - Site-only copy: `apps/web/`
   - Skills: `packages/<category>/<name>/skills/`
   - Recipes: `packages/ai/ai-knowledge/knowledge/recipes.yaml` + `pnpm knowledge:sync`
2. Package docs are **source of truth**; web renders from `packages/<category>/*/docs`.
3. **Delete** `_ai-docs/wip/<topic>/` after promotion.
4. Do not leave WIP notes as the only documentation.

## Do not

- Put final user-facing docs only in `_ai-docs/`
- Create root-level `_ai-docs/<topic>/` (use `wip/<topic>/` only)
- Duplicate `roadmap/`, package docs, or `knowledge/*.md` in WIP
- Commit secrets into AI notes
- Skip ai-knowledge because "docs were enough"
- Scatter cross-cutting facts across many stub files (see `.cursor/rules/docs-depth-tokens.mdc`)
